/-!
# The crossing gluing residual in the physical negative-one carrier

An actual half-critical crossing already generates a canonical finite core,
ordered primitive half-critical component sources, and the complete cross/tail
gluing row left after all component self rows are materialized.  This module
places that exact row in the existing whole nonlinear `H⁻¹` carrier before any
coefficient quotient is taken.

The construction is not a new occurrence metric.  It subtracts the generated
finite-component self forcing from the actual whole nonlinear forcing in the
same physical negative-one space.  The inverse-Laplacian observation is
faithful on this residual: the zero mode is forced to vanish by the actual
transverse law, and every nonzero Fourier weight is invertible.  Consequently
the native source residual is nonzero exactly when its physical `H⁻¹` image is
nonzero.

No residual, nonzero witness, cutoff, component count, target state, payment
bound, or continuation certificate enters a producer mouth.
-/

